More than validation
description: the role is description, not just checking - hence meta, not schema
- >
  A JSON Schema exists to validate. A yamlover meta's role is wider: it **describes** - typing,
  decoding, rendering, presentation - and validation is a secondary, optional use of the same
  description ([metadata first](*::language:principles:metadata-first)). That is why the language is
  called **yamlover meta**, not yamlover schema: `title` and `description` are not annotation
  afterthoughts bolted onto a validator - the metadata is the point, and the validator reads it too.
